;; Regression coverage for ISS-641: instantiation cost on modules
;; with thousands of distinct types.
;;
;; The type section below is a chain of distinct singleton function
;; types (distinct parameter arities for the first thirteen, then
;; distinct typed references to earlier types), followed by one
;; struct type whose default value is allocated by a global
;; initializer. On the pre-ISS-641 type registry this module spent
;; minutes in instantiation before executing a single instruction;
;; it must stay well inside the WAST runner per-file timeout.
